{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-2812"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of fluid power equipment"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "2812"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :fluid-power/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :pressure-safety :hydraulic-fluid-safety :equipment-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :fluid-power-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :eda :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "FluidPowerAdvisor ⊣ Fluid Power Equipment Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS
 COORDINATION actor for hydraulic/pneumatic fluid-power-equipment
 manufacturing (machining/assembly/pressure-test-bench lines producing
 finished hydraulic pumps, hydraulic cylinders, hydraulic valves,
 hydraulic motors, pneumatic cylinders and pneumatic valves) -- not
 direct machining/assembly-line-equipment control authority and not
 pressure-safety-certification authority (e.g. ASME BPVC / PED
 2014/68/EU pressure-equipment conformity mark or ISO 4413/ISO 4414
 fluid-power-system safety compliance mark). Four ops
 (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance` /
 `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Twelve concrete governor checks elaborate this
 blueprint's four HARD invariants: propose-only effect, closed op
 allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct machining/
 assembly-line-equipment control), permanent equipment-actuate block,
 permanent pressure-safety-certification-authority block (this actor
 never self-issues a pressure-equipment conformity or fluid-power-
 system safety compliance mark), independent equipment verification/
 registration before maintenance scheduling, independent batch
 verification/registration before shipment coordination, independent
 shipment-quantity recompute against the batch's own logged production
 quantity, double-schedule guard, product-type validation,
 pressure-test plausibility validation, and defect-rate plausibility
 validation. Safety-concern flagging (pressure-rating/hydraulic-fluid-
 safety concern) ALWAYS escalates to a human plant supervisor;
 `:log-production-batch` is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and
 only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
